RIGGING RULES (critical): every part is a SEPARATE piece with a wide empty gap (at least 70px) from every other piece, nothing touching or overlapping, no part cut by the image edge. Arm segments are drawn perfectly STRAIGHT and VERTICAL with the shoulder/elbow joint end at the TOP, and both ends of each arm segment get a rounded cap so overlapping joints hide seams. Where a part attaches to another (neck, shoulders, tail base), extend it a little with a rounded overlap tab instead of a hard cut. Keep every part at the SAME scale it has on the reference character. Same colors, patches and details as the reference.
Art style: exactly the reference: Tim Burton-like gothic, Don't Starve Together-like hand-drawn 2D paper cutout look, rough consistent-weight thick black outline around every shape, paper-grain texture INSIDE the shapes, low saturation muted palette.
BACKGROUND RULE (critical): the background must be ONE perfectly flat solid pure chroma-key green (#00FF00) everywhere, no gradient, no texture, no vignette, no drop shadows, no ground shadow, no motion lines, no sparkles, no text, no labels, no numbers. Do not use any green color inside the artwork itself.
